<title>UK: SOCCER-COLLATED RESULTS OF WORLD CUP EUROPEAN GROUP QUALIFIERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-COLLATED RESULTS OF WORLD CUP EUROPEAN GROUP QUALIFIERS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results of World Cup</p>
<p>soccer European group qualifiers on Wednesday:</p>
<p>Group one</p>
<p>In Copenhagen: Denmark 2 Greece 2-1 (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Denmark - Theodoros Zagorakis (25th min, own goal),</p>
<p>Brian Laudrup (50th)</p>
<p>Greece - Georgios Donis (35th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,226</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p>In Perugia: Italy 1 Georgia 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Fabrizio Ravanelli (42nd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 16,146</p>
<p>In London: England 2 Poland 1 (2-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>England - Alan Shearer (24th, 37th)</p>
<p>Poland - Marek Citko (6th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 74,663</p>
<p>Group three</p>
<p>In Oslo: Norway 3 Hungary 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Kjetil Rekdal (83rd, 89th, 90th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 22,480</p>
<p>Group four</p>
<p>In Tallinn: Estonia 0 Scotland 0 - match abandoned after</p>
<p>three seconds.</p>
<p>In Minsk: Belarus 1 Latvia 1-1 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Belarus - Vladimir Makovsky (78th)</p>
<p>Latvia - Mikhail Zemlitsky (16th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000</p>
<p>In Stockholm: Sweden 0 Austria 1 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorer: Andreas Herzog (11th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 36,859</p>
<p>Group five</p>
<p>In Tel Aviv: Israel 1 Russia 1</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Israel - Gadi Brumer (64th)</p>
<p>Russia: Igor Kolivanov (79th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 38,000</p>
<p>Group six</p>
<p>In Prague: Czech Republic 0 Spain 0 </p>
<p>Attendance: 19,223</p>
<p>Group seven</p>
<p>In Serravalle: San Marino 0 Belgium 3 (0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers: Gert Verheyen (10th), Luc NIlis (20th, 46th)</p>
<p>Attendance - 1,353</p>
<p>Group eight</p>
<p>In Vilnius: Lithuania beat Liechtenstein 2-1 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Lithuania - Edgaras Jankauskas (43rd), Arminas Narbekovas</p>
<p>(55th)</p>
<p>Liechtenstein - Harry Zech (53rd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000</p>
<p>In Dublin: Ireland 3 Macedonia 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Jason McAteer (8th min), Tony Cascarino (47th,</p>
<p>70th).</p>
<p>Attendance: 31,600</p>
<p>In Reykjavik: Iceland 0, Romania 4 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers: Dino Moldovan (22nd), Gheorghe Hagi (60th),</p>
<p>Gheorghe Popescu (75th), Dan Petrescu (89th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,000</p>
<p>Group nine</p>
<p>In Tirana: Albania 0 Portugal 3 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers: Luis Figo (11th minute), Helder Cristovao (77th),</p>
<p>Rui Costa (89th).</p>
<p>Attendance: 10,000</p>
<p>In Yerevan: Armenia 1 Germany 5 (0-3)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Armenia - Mikaelyan (85th)</p>
<p>Germany - Haessler (20th, 39th), Klinsmann (26th), Bobic</p>
<p>(69th), Kuntz (80th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 50,000</p>
</text>
